{"kind":"report","text":"Approved as an evidence-only joint planning handoff: the owned byte-identical copies of exact 017 Draft2 (primary dacc7d85), exact reconciled018 (769207de), and their identity manifest46364275, at common head345012d0d0ef6abb92c6a6f42c3318d55a5d3c92, under ordinary replacement invitatione05aecb5 and my promise59e27459. The demo-first sequence, composable scope/lane direction and complete retarget/removal obligation agree with Hugh's d4e07064 direction. No blocking defect remains in these two planning inputs. This verdict approves their planning scope and ownership map; D1–D8 mechanisms still require their own exact design decisions and applicable independent review/adoption before implementation. It grants no source, wire, runtime, capacity, deployment or release approval.\n\nComplete evidence. I read every byte of both frozen attachments: 017 at eed189e37b8a9ffff1f03feaf512be2525aefe39:attachments/2026-10-04-composable-lanes-and-github-demo-draft2.md, 690 lines,47,895 bytes, SHA256 a1302d02f26495fba35955fd570a4da09bd67b511f5787165206df309596bf88; and018 at 8df56a194e05c48cc1ae1181c3aa9c887f7951e4:attachments/2026-10-04-composable-lanes-task-ledger-draft2.md,238 lines,22,650 bytes, SHA256 1ac551d6281f7a09e952d3f9d749e2133ace083f096fd5ed38e0f0de8852bf2b. Independent retained-byte identities match these hashes. The three new bundle subjects and new invitation/promise are current. I independently verified their raw event payloads, head/path, raw Rests-On provenance, Git blobs, exact lengths and SHA256; both full copies compare equal to the originals above. I read the complete1,754-byte manifest (SHA2565d94551c997f95cf4a0f419d6f80c416b81905bcc32791200f99ff2a0222c688). The isolated registered checkout is clean at345012d0. The requester replaced the old invitation through authorized act474a5e3d, and I reconciled my old accepted promise through my own authorized act2099acea; all assessed scope continues unchanged. No original artifact/attachment was reheaded or superseded. Ordinary evidence-only prepare binds to original planning request5c716a5c and confers no implementation closure. I also read the original full R0–R4 conditions and S1–S4 disposition acts, refreshed their current commitments, and cross-checked all three complete browser stories in planning-owned005 as contextual acceptance rather than successor mechanism approval. No source or application execution was performed.\n\nArchitecture. A scope owns local ordering, state fold and admission. A lane carries the full issue/work/PR conversation: exact intent, discussion, several contributions and commitments, negotiation, handover, qualified review and outcomes. It can precede any hold; lease expiry cannot erase intent or responsibility. Issue and PR retain familiar distinct identities while their work path remains linked. Membership/configuration/destination scopes use the substrate without being mislabeled work lanes. The repository view composes source positions and causal facts; it is not an ordering authority merely because the UI presents one repository.\n\nD1 and D5 are properly assigned to R1 and the contract/log/policy owners. Identity, incarnation, reference classes, receipts, retained opening/transition meaning, replay inputs, bounded reads/checkpoints and complete local dependency validation remain concrete design outputs. Parallel preparation must validate named dependencies, absence/range predicates, authority and time at commit. The current conservative whole-head rule is not removed on the strength of prose. Reference validation, reproducible state reconstruction and audit history within the new model remain required; no old Artroom reader, format, engine or client compatibility is added.\n\nD4 and D6 are assigned to R2 with lifecycle/UI/public-package owners, driven by R0's complete person-facing scenario. Source-owned links, child-creation intent/receipt, revisioned delivery, cycle handling and exact close/reopen/unlink ordering are named obligations. A changed goal explicitly renegotiates affected promises. A required failed child remains unresolved until an authorized replacement or scope decision. Joining freezes selected contribution identities, artifact versions, expected destination base and the combined commit/tree. Later child work cannot float into that manifest. Git text compatibility does not prove interface correctness. Child checks and approvals retain their subjects and count only through an explicit equivalence/carry policy; the combined failure scenario and qualified review remain mandatory.\n\nD2 and D3 belong to R3 and the actual authority/Git/effect owners. Exact historical facts, current grants and operation commitments are separate. Locally verifiable authority needs a specified freshness/revocation boundary, unavailable behavior, compromise handling and retained proof. A signature or cached roster alone cannot establish current permission; ordinary admission must not synchronously traverse a universal parent graph. Publication needs the exact PR/source commitment and destination reservation to agree on result, authority, evidence and expected base. Cancellation ordering, the abortable/irrevocable boundary and writer fencing must be selected before implementation. An unknown push stays unresolved through same-operation retry/readback; timeout, cancellation and model prose cannot prove it absent. Neither the reference protocol nor several current reads establishes a general distributed transaction.\n\nSecurity. A relationship is not a grant. Child creation and imported activity retain the initiating actor's admitted intent and cannot invent another participant's signature. Review independence includes selected contributors and conflict-resolution authors, rather than only the final integrator label. Coding environments remain isolated from publisher/checker credentials and private environments. Current read/control authority, last-key loss, member removal, grantor revocation and admitted-result settlement have different consequences. Credential and effect retirement remains with the actual owner. Removing an old runtime, API or storage format cannot delete a real unresolved duty.\n\nAll three browser outcomes are retained in useful scope: durable coding/checkpoint recovery, the complete browser task/watch/steer/attention/pause/cancel/review/publication journey, and same-member continuity across devices. Acknowledged edits, completed command results and prepared Git objects must survive the selected recovery boundary; host loss does not preserve process memory or make arbitrary shell effects safe to retry. Device B continues the same authorized work after A leaves, while an uninvited browser is refused. One-device revocation, loss of the owner's last active key, member removal and agent-authority loss have distinct controls and outcomes. Conversation output, saved work, accepted proposal, eligibility, confirmed Git publication and any separate requester judgment remain distinct authoritative facts. These acceptance outcomes survive retargeting;005's old Room, key-storage, checkpoint, client and deployment arrangements are not implicitly adopted.\n\nD7 and D8 remain owned. R4 must specify the useful per-test invariants and selected fidelity boundaries, complete race/causal-replay evidence and an agreed one/ten/hundred-lane workload with shared-destination and hot-lane variants. Storage segmentation does not remove a hot authority bottleneck. Control/revocation paths, indexes, fan-out, backlog/recovery, latency distributions, CPU/storage and cost belong in the measurement. The cited provider descriptions and historical test-economy results are not a successor throughput, cost or correctness result. R0/planner and every affected owner must complete the exact path/export/configuration/test/document/repository census and issue actual successor/removal work.\n\nP0–P8 and A1–A10 remain complete. P0's compelling scenario drives P1 reference/admission, P2 complete lifecycle and P3 authority/publication choices; P4 supplies a real distributed proof, P5 the familiar application and public install, and P6 deployed/cold-person/replay/full-guide acceptance. P7 retargets every retained application/component, and P8 establishes removal and one active model. A1 familiar use, A2 work before hold, A3 exact split/join, A4 failing combined correctness, A5 delayed/out-of-order references, A6 both authority/cancellation race orders, A7 unrelated-lane isolation and writer fencing, A8 chosen-model causal replay, A9 measured capacity and A10 exhaustive owned alignment/removal are all present and assigned. The familiar screen/action/filter/branch-rule/merge subset and intentional independence/carry differences must be explicit. Broader GitHub features may be decided individually; the current inventory is not a claim of complete service equivalence.\n\nCommitment reconciliation. The requester explicitly retired S1 in 0de4b3a0 after the raced promise aa601cab defeated the unclaimed replacement guard. Current authoritative inspection projects both the request and that commitment as cancelled. That is cancellation, not delivery, personal promise retraction or reinterpretation as R1. The act expressly asks for original-commitment reconciliation; I have not found or credited a separate builder termination report. R1 has its own separately accepted promise 8d614272. Any remaining reconciliation belongs in the owned formal-disposition ledger before closure. S2–S4 were unclaimed and explicitly retired by 175b3ad1,22aeb1a0 and ac896b1b; R2–R4 are distinct accepted design requests. Other accepted promises require their own attributed disposition. The category table does not cancel them, satisfy external duties or deliver their replacements.\n\nCurrent state is later than018's frozen snapshot: R2–R4 now have accepted promises8da8b218,8661af6b and f3c5d607. R0's original request remains effective, while its reported delivery/earlier independent verdict require current-provenance refresh before adoption. My full six-artifact R0 source/document review was separate; its historical approval92abd211 is not a current joint or source approval. R1–R4 detailed reports and amendments retain their own review path. In particular, my full R1 design review at665e490b requests corrections to delivery-derived child identity, multiple same-entry relationship updates and the timed drain protocol, with a live/retained bounded-read clarification owned withR4. The normal R1 verdictd3b3b041 includes all mandatory historical news and inherits their staleness; current direct-source finding447c7846 records the independently checked exact-byte triggers. This planning approval does not settle those corrections or adopt that contract. This joint verdict does not preapprove their unresolved technical choices or mark promised design, source or removal work delivered.\n\nSimplification and breadth of value. Use one reusable primitive/meaning/reference system across agents, people, views and verification. Keep ordinary product language in the experience; expose exact subjects and honest uncertainty where they affect decisions. Avoid a hidden demo serializer, parallel fold/publication engine or an unowned cleanup bucket. Removal is part of each replacement's acceptance. Retained examples, Jam, collections/firm/control, substrate, Git, agents, browser/client/CLI/MCP, checker jobs, exports/scripts/locks, deployment bindings, fixtures/runners and active guides each need a useful witness or explicit retirement/defer disposition. Other Artroom repositories and real credentials/effects are included in the inventory. Woo, atseq and the gitseq tracking service remain outside this commissioning; production rollout implementation is excluded, with future alignment recorded separately.\n\nDisposition. Proceed with the complete design work and incremental implementation after the relevant exact decisions are independently reviewed and adopted. No schedule estimate reduces useful acceptance, full browser recovery, causal verification or A10 removal. The outstanding contract choices, per-test/source inventory, formal promise/effect dispositions, implementation and deployed evidence remain assigned work, not hidden exceptions. This fulfils the unchanged full joint review through replacement invitatione05aecb5. It is a normal guarded evidence-only planning verdict with017 first and all three common-head subjects, not a mergeable implementation verdict. The owned bundle preserves the two original frozen attachment facts and their distinct original commits.\n\nThe same standing checker task is user-resumed; its restored active execution was independently observed in 20ce53a3. This review consists of benign document/static-provenance work. The earlier rejected private diagnostic was not rerun, rewritten, extended or delegated; no reviewer/task/model/backend replacement or restriction override was used. No install, typecheck, test, probe, credential/provider effect, deployment or live-person contact was performed.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dacc7d8580433d299ef49d5eff16633367dd60eb","binding":"evidence-only","head":"345012d0d0ef6abb92c6a6f42c3318d55a5d3c92","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:59e27459ba00c0b20df5d8e609bd612a6c7c218e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2099acea66d8f46bd5099cbac5ea21dbf191f1d8","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}